# API and HTTP Patterns

This project uses a custom HTTP client for API calls.

## HTTP Client

- HTTP client is in `src/lib/http/index.ts`
- Use `http<T>()` function for API calls
- Generic type parameter for response type

## API Call Pattern

```typescript
import http from '@/lib/http';
import type { User } from '@/entities/User/User.type';

const res = await http<User>({
  url: '/v1/auth/login',
  method: 'POST',
  body: data,
});

if (res.data) {
  // Handle success
}
```

## Error Handling

- Wrap API calls in try-catch blocks
- Use `toast.error()` from `sonner` for error notifications
- Handle validation errors from Zod schemas before API calls

## Validation Before API Calls

Always validate data with Zod schemas before making API calls:

```typescript
const error = schema.safeParse(data);
if (error.error) {
  // Handle validation errors
} else {
  // Make API call
  const res = await http({ ... });
}
```

## TanStack Query

- Use TanStack Query for server state management when appropriate
- QueryClient is configured in `src/app/query-client.tsx`
- Use QueryClientProvider from root layout

